our company name is called pine biotech  we're a biotechnology company located in  the u.s and new orleans in louisiana  but we are a technology transfer company  that stems out of university of haifa  specifically the center  for bioinformatics called the tower  bioinformatics research center  the center was started to make  bioinformatics more accessible  design algorithms as well as make them  useful for people that do not have  extensive bioinformatics background and  expertise  and what we've identified as a team is  that there is a  growing need in training individuals to  be effective at utilizing  the wide arrange of bioinformatics tools  and apply them in a meaningful way to  research  challenges that are pressing in the area  of biomedical research  agriculture and biotechnology and so as  a result in 2017 we started a program  that  up till date has over 15 000  participants from around the world  we have a lot of content that we have  refined with the help of many different  curriculum reviewers and work together  with a number of  highly specialized universities around  the world  organizations that are training the next  generation of bioinformaticians  and working with statewide and  country-wide  organizations that are designed to help  elevate the level of biomedical research  around the country  including the louisiana biomedical  research network  including our partners in different high  schools colleges  research labs and industry  and so as a result we have really  identified these three pillars  of our program which is access to big  data in a meaningful way so solving the  problem  of computational resources so that  anyone from the comfort of their home  can utilize complex tools apply them to  big data and get meaningful insights  the second aspect is mentorship it's not  easy from the comfort of your home  to really know what you're doing and so  that's why we brought in  a number of experienced and highly  qualified mentors that are ready to  assist  anyone go from knowing about  bioinformatics  to actually applying bioinformatics and  the third pillar is obviously training  so we provide  resources that are making the  computational background the algorithmic  component  training in coding and different  elements of  bioinformatics as well as biology and  biomedicine and biotechnology how  do you apply data science to these  challenges so we merge those together  in our omics logic curriculum
 

